se,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"The answer covers all three requested inquiry areas.\\n\\n- **Selection:** it asks about the rationale for choosing the LMM/exchange, alternatives considered, conflicts, and capacity under stress.\\n- **Relevant-market expertise:** it asks about asset-class track record, staffing and continuity, and spread, depth and NBBO metrics.\\n- **Capital and seed support:** it asks whether the seed is temporary market-maker inventory, how and when it unwinds, and whether quoting continues after withdrawal.\\n\\nIt separates temporary seed from lasting investor assets and asks what drives retention of those assets. That implicitly acknowledges investors may leave, though it never says outright that lasting assets are not permanent or that subsidized investors can exit. It also covers fee-sharing incentives and termination effects.\\n\\nIt frames the list as suggested inquiry rather than mandatory approval criteria. Phrasing it as \\\"Is the seed...\\\" avoids implying that every LMM provides seed. Capital commitments are covered only indirectly, through the stress-capacity and seed questions.\\n\\nNeither gap is material, and there is no factual error.\"}","ttft_ms":2497,"type":"result","duration_ms":6341,"uuid":"f911f8bb-34de-451f-93ea-5635e3aad32d","ttft_stream_ms":521,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":521,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
